OL,3,GNEWSAWe saw signs of domestic abuse,
OL,4,Abut we didn't know how to protect Stacy
OL,5,
OL,6,FStacy Hunter's family saw clear signs
OL,7,Fthat she was being manipulated,
OL,8,Fcontrolled and abused by her estranged
OL,9,Fhusband Jim Mair long before he
OL,10,Fmurdered her.
OL,12,FMair "dictated" what was happening in
OL,13,FStacy's life, used her three children
OL,14,Fas leverage, threatened suicide, and
OL,15,Ftook his violent temper out on objects
OL,16,Fin the house - without laying a hand on
OL,17,FStacy directly.
OL,19,FHer brother Sean wanted to intervene
OL,20,Fand help her, but he worried about
OL,21,Fbeing too "full on" and potentially
OL,22,Fcausing more harm.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
